      "claim": "Direct in vivo records for imatinib show poor CNS access: CSF concentrations were <5% of plasma (often 1-2%) and PET showed no brain uptake, with P-gp-mediated efflux limiting brain distribution.",
      "card_ids": ["C03","C05","C06","C14","C29"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "CGP74588, the active N-desmethyl imatinib metabolite, also had low brain uptake restricted by Bcrp1 and CSF <5% of plasma.",
      "card_ids": ["C07","C18","C26"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Structurally close aminopyrimidine-amide kinase inhibitors had very low unbound brain exposure (Bu/Pu 0.08-0.11) and one showed an MDR1 efflux ratio of 6.8, indicating efflux-limited CNS exposure in this chemotype.",
      "card_ids": ["C10","C11","C15","C28"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 efflux records show imatinib and brigatinib are P-gp/Bcrp substrates, with brain exposure increased 4- to 28-fold (imatinib) and 20.7-fold (brigatinib) in knockout mice; this supports high efflux liability for the query's basic aminopyrimidine-piperazine-piperidine scaffold, though it is not a direct outcome measurement.",
      "card_ids": ["C42","C44","C45","C46","C48","C52","C53"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Other efflux-prone, high-TPSA inhibitors (CZC25146, GSK2982772, SB258585) showed negligible or low brain penetration, consistent with a fail outcome.",
      "card_ids": ["C12","C13","C17","C25","C27"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "efflux_transport",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C42","C43","C44","C45","C46","C47","C48","C49","C50","C51","C52","C53"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct brain/plasma, CSF, Kp,uu, PET, or in situ perfusion measurement for the exact query molecule.",
    "No query-specific P-gp/Bcrp/MDR1 efflux assay or directional transport measurement.",
    "No query-specific passive-permeability (PAMPA/Caco-2) measurement.",
    "Analog evidence comes from related but not identical aminopyrimidine scaffolds; no same-scaffold positive CNS control.",
    "L4 efflux records are mostly mouse knockout/elacridar studies for imatinib, brigatinib, and doxazosin, not direct human CNS exposure outcomes for the query."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted fail. The query is a large (MW 570.7), high-TPSA (97.4), polybasic (neutral fraction 0.09) aminopyrimidine-piperazine-piperidine amide with high efflux liability. Direct and close-analog in vivo records for imatinib/CGP74588 and related aminopyrimidine-amide kinase inhibitors show poor CNS exposure (CSF <5% plasma, PET no brain uptake, Bu/Pu 0.08-0.11). L4 efflux records confirm imatinib and brigatinib are P-gp/Bcrp substrates with large knockout-induced brain-exposure increases, supporting the efflux-liability interpretation, but efflux substrate status alone is not outcome-defining and these are not query-specific measurements. The fail decision is kept and modestly strengthened; confidence remains moderate because no direct query CNS-exposure or efflux assay is available."
}

